' Merge index of a failed offered deploy (DR-115, bug 10986).
' A user failure rolls back the user events U of the deploy log and keeps the
' settlement: the wallet settlement events W and the receipt events R. The
' operation journal of the committed evidence fixes U, and replay binds the same
' prefix. The merge index takes log[U..] with the stored wallet map, so a block
' in a merged branch brings its charge into the merged state, or the merge
' rejects its chain with a record.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-115);
'                  casper/src/rust/merging/block_index.rs (committed_log);
'                  casper/src/rust/util/rholang/costacc/offered_evidence.rs
'                  (failed_offered_committed_suffix, committed_user_event_count).
' Formal model:    formal/rocq/cost_accounted_rho/theories/FailedSettlementMergeIndex.v;
'                  formal/tlaplus/cost_accounted_rho/FailedSettlementMergeIndex.tla.
' Palette:  rolled back = reject red · empty segment = delta amber · committed = pool green
'           evidence = supply blue · index rule = gate teal · merge = process lilac
'           kept charge = note green · rejection record = note red
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/failed-offered-merge-index.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh failed-offered-merge-index.puml)

@startuml failed-offered-merge-index
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #333333
skinparam PackageBorderColor #666666
title Merge index of a failed offered deploy (DR-115)

package "Block A: one failed offered deploy" $ca_pkg_amber {
  rectangle "**deploy log**, <latex>n</latex> events, in this order\n|<$ca_rejectfill> **U**: user events, positions <latex>[0, U)</latex>, rolled back |<$ca_delta> **G**: grant-issue events, empty for a user failure |<$ca_pool> **W**: wallet settlement, positions <latex>[U, U + W)</latex>, committed |<$ca_pool> **R**: receipts, positions <latex>[U + W, n)</latex>, committed |" as LOG $ca_note_grey
  rectangle "stored mergeable map\nwallet channels only" as MAP $ca_pool
}

rectangle "committed native cost evidence\noperation journal: <latex>U = \sum_{j} w(j)</latex>\n<latex>w</latex>: Rejected 0, Stored 1, Matched 2\nwallet_settlement_log_events = W" as EV $ca_supply

rectangle "**committed_log()**\nsuccess: the whole log\nfailed legacy: none (the dev rule)\nfailed offered: <latex>\mathrm{log}[U..]</latex>\nfails closed on a decode error\nor when <latex>n - U < W</latex>" as CL $ca_gate

rectangle "**DeployIndex** of A\nevents: W then R\nnumber channels: the wallet map" as DI $ca_process

rectangle "**DagMerger.merge**\nbase block: its post-state holds the charge\nbranch block: apply the kept chain,\nor reject it with a record" as MERGE $ca_process

rectangle "merged pre-state keeps\nthe payer debit, the fee,\nthe receipts and the\nprepaid consumption" as KEPT $ca_note_green
rectangle "rejection record\n(the deploy is not applied;\nowner recovery is gap G6)" as REC $ca_note_red

EV -[$ca_instantiate]-> CL : boundary U\n(the replay decode)
LOG -[$ca_credit]-> CL : W then R are indexed\nU is not indexed
CL -[$ca_credit]-> DI : events W then R
MAP -[$ca_credit]-> DI : number channels
DI -[$ca_neutral]-> MERGE
MERGE -[$ca_credit]-> KEPT : chain kept
MERGE -[$ca_debit]-> REC : chain conflicts

note bottom of CL
  Replay binds the same prefix <latex>\mathrm{log}[..U]</latex>
  to the native user trace (native_user_event_count),
  so the merge and replay use one boundary.
end note

legend right
  red: rolled back · amber: empty segment · green: committed
  blue: committed evidence · teal: the index rule · lilac: merge
endlegend
@enduml
